# The two pieces the holding app was missing (m2/economy-gaps): the LIVING
# family's bunk, which was an empty heading on the slate, and a SECOND generator,
# so the wind is no longer the only power in the game.
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/holding-living.tour --seed=1 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0 \
#     --give=timber:6,reeds:6,rag:6,wick:4,scrap:10,copper:4
#
# (Everything is built here on the real keys out of the creel — nothing is staged
# with --holding, because the whole claim is that a player can now put these two
# up. The hour is daylight on purpose: an array makes nothing after dark, which is
# the point of it, so a tour that proved it at midnight would prove the opposite.)
coast calm
wait 0.6
shot 01-empty-ground-and-a-full-creel with land:coast
# The LIVING family used to be a heading with nothing under it.
tap holding
await app:holding 4
wait 0.4
shot 02-the-living-family-has-a-piece-in-it with app:holding
choose build_bunk
tap use
await made 8
tap pause
await piece:bunk 6
wait 0.6
shot 03-a-bunk-stands-and-its-berths-can-be-seen with piece:bunk, holding
# Room for the next piece, so it is not put up inside the last one.
walk 1,0 1.2
wait 0.4
# The other generator. A spinner is free and unreliable; an array is dear and
# dependable, right up until the sun goes down.
tap holding
await app:holding 4
choose build_solar_array
tap use
await made 8
tap pause
await piece:solar_array 6
wait 0.6
shot 04-panels-raked-at-the-sun with piece:solar_array, holding
# And something for it to run, to prove the power is real and not a number in a
# table: a mast has no hands on it and no wind behind it, only daylight.
walk 1,0 1.2
wait 0.4
tap holding
await app:holding 4
choose build_radio_mast
tap use
await made 8
tap pause
await powered 10
wait 0.6
shot 05-a-mast-running-on-daylight-alone with piece:solar_array, piece:radio_mast, powered
